# =============================================================================
# Docker build context for the Yekis container image.
# =============================================================================
#
# Everything excluded here is either rebuilt inside the image, never shipped,
# or must never enter the build context. The last category is the important
# one: a context that carries .env files and private keys is a context where a
# secret can be baked into a layer and pushed to a registry.

# ── Dependencies and build output ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image. Copying a host node_modules into a
# Linux image is also a functional bug, not just a size problem: the host
# tree holds Windows binaries.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
apps/frontend/dist/
apps/backend/dist/

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# ── Runtime data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uploaded chat attachments, evidence bundles and the local-disk fallback
# copies. They belong to a running instance, never to an image.
apps/backend/uploads/
**/uploads/
backups/
*.dump
*.sql

# ── Repository metadata and local state ─────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.deepcode/
logs/
scratch/
resource_to_read/
node_modules/.cache/

# ── Documentation, tests and audits ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Not needed to build or run the image. The docs live in the repository and
# in docs/; the deployment runbook is docs/ALETCLOUD_DEPLOYMENT.md.
docs/
**/*.md
security/
apps/backend/tests/
apps/frontend/src/**/*.test.ts
apps/frontend/src/**/*.test.tsx

# ── Editor and OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
